WEBVTT

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.620
Tom had a restaurant in the center of the
city.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:09.160
He also had a big problem. Business was
down, and he had many bills to pay.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.500
Tom was worried. He didn't want to lose
his restaurant.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:18.500
Tom loved running. He ran every morning
before work.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.340
He was one of the fastest runners in
town.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.660
One evening, his friend Paul told him
about a big race.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.520
"The winner gets thirty thousand euros,"
Paul said.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.420
"Why don't you run?" Tom thought about
the money.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.940
He could pay his bills and save his
restaurant.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.300
The next day, he entered the race, but
there was a problem.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.620
His friend Martin also entered. Martin
was from the same running club.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.460
He was the only runner in the club who
was faster than Tom.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.480
Tom wanted to win, but he was worried
about Martin.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:58.220
On Friday, Tom and Martin went to the
city.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.440
They stayed at the same hotel in one
room.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.340
On Saturday evening, they had dinner
together.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.240
"Are you ready for tomorrow?" Martin
asked.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.180
"Yes," Tom answered. "I think it will be
a good race," Martin said.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:18.340
Tom smiled, but he was not happy. At ten
o'clock, they went back to their room.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.000
Martin put his running shoes near the
door.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:26.400
"Good night, Tom." "Good night." An hour
later, Martin was asleep.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.520
Tom got out of bed. He looked at Martin's
shoes.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:36.500
He took a small knife from his bag. Then
he made a small cut in one shoe.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:42.220
The cut was difficult to see. Tom wanted
Martin to have problems with his shoe.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.780
He wanted him to run more slowly. He put
the knife away and went back to bed.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:52.800
On Sunday morning, they got up early.
Martin put on his shoes.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.540
"Ready?" he asked. "Yes," Tom said. At
nine o'clock, the race

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.440
started. For the first fifteen
kilometers, they ran together.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.220
Then Martin ran faster. Soon, Tom
couldn't see him.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.680
At twenty kilometers, Tom saw Martin
again.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.880
Martin was running slowly. "What's
wrong?" Tom asked.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:20.220
"My foot hurts. I think there's a problem
with my shoe." "Maybe you should stop."

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:26.080
"No, I want to finish." Tom ran on. At
twenty-eight kilometers, he

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.260
heard people shouting. He looked back.
Martin was on the road.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.700
He couldn't get up. Two people ran to
help him.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.260
Tom stopped for a moment. Then he looked
at the runners in front of him.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.800
He ran on. At thirty-five kilometers, Tom
was second.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.820
He was tired, but he ran faster. At forty
kilometers, he passed the first runner.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:53.740
Now he was first. A few minutes later, he
finished the race.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.140
He won thirty thousand euros. People took
photos.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.900
A woman gave him a medal. Tom was very
happy.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.480
Later, he went back to the hotel. Martin
was not there.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:11.860
Tom called him, but there was no answer.
At six o'clock, he got a message,

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:17.420
"I'm in hospital. My foot is broken. I
can't run for six months."

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.820
Tom read the message again. He sat on his
bed.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:27.220
He didn't want this to happen. He only
wanted Martin to run more slowly.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.480
The next morning, Tom went to the
hospital.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:35.100
Martin was in bed. "Congratulations,"
Martin said.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.980
"Thanks. How are you?" "Not good. My shoe
broke.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.660
I fell, and now my foot is broken." Tom
looked at the floor.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:50.240
Martin looked at him. "It's strange. My
shoe was fine on Saturday."

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.440
Tom said nothing. "You were in our room
that night.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.060
Did you see anything?" Tom looked at
Martin.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:04.540
For a minute, he didn't speak. Then he
said, "Yes, I cut your shoe."

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:10.740
Martin looked at him in surprise. "You?
Why?" "I needed the money.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.180
I wanted you to run more slowly. I'm
sorry." Martin was quiet.

00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:21.500
Then he said, "Please go, Tom." Tom left
the hospital.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:24.840
A few months later, business was good
again.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.820
Tom paid his bills and bought new tables
for his restaurant.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.200
He had no more money problems. But Martin
never spoke to him again.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:38.600
He didn't answer Tom's calls. They were
no longer friends.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:44.740
Tom was no longer afraid of losing his
restaurant, but to save his business, he

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.399
lost something much more important.